e can run the model. Now, design. Look at existing \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m\u001b[3mcategory code. We need a new module perhaps \u001b[38;5;153msrc/review/\u001b[39m (or \u001b[38;5;153msrc/clarity/\u001b[39m). Let's \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m\u001b[3mthink names. The CLI command is \u001b[38;5;153mreview\u001b[39m. Types: \u001b[38;5;153mts export interface LineVerdict { \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[2m\u001b[3minvoice: string; // maybe line: string; clear: boolean; why: string; } \u001b[39m Prompt: \u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m\u001b[3msystem prompt for line clarity. The model gets lines of one invoice and returns JSON \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m     \u001b[2m\u001b[3mlist with verdict (\u001b[38;5;153mclear\u001b[39m/\u001b[38;5;153mvague\u001b[39m) and why for each. Need robust parsing. Let's consider\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bwhat Maria's data says. We should craft prompt based on her grades. The eval set has\r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m\u001b[3m40 cases, each one line independently. The review command operates per invoice \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m     \u001b[2m\u001b[3m(multiple lines). The model evaluation should ideally mirror the actual request \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bformat. The scoring script should run the same function used by command:…\r\u001b[2B\u001b[23m\u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;174m✶\u001b[3GNebulizin\u001b[38;5;216mg…\u001b[38;5;174m \u001b[38;5;246m(1m 14s · ↓\u001b[27G15.2k tokens · thought for 46s)\r\u001b[1B  ⎿  Tip: Use /btw to\u001b[23Gask a quick side question without interrupting Claude's current work\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H\u001b[H\r\u001b[27B\u001b[38;5;174m✻\u001b[39m\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
